# programs/native_rg_alias_e2e.cyr — 4.5.0: render-graph transients sharing one backing
# allocation on native AMD, checked on the Cezanne.
#
# rg_build_ctx gives a native graph's transients one GTT BO; with rg_aliasing(g, 1),
# transients with disjoint lifetimes share bytes, and rg_execute_mq makes each node that
# reuses a slot wait for every queue that used the slot's previous occupant.
#   A. A compute chain across rings: n0 (COMPUTE) b1 = b0 + 1, n1 (GRAPHICS) b2 = b1 + 1,
#      n2 (COMPUTE) b3 = b2 + 1. b2 reuses b0's bytes and b3 reuses b1's, so 4 buffers fit
#      in 2 slots. Every b3[i] must be b0[i] + 3.
#   B. The case only the reuse wait covers: two INDEPENDENT nodes on different rings. n0
#      (GRAPHICS) runs a 32768-step loop, then reads X into a buffer it owns; n1 (COMPUTE)
#      writes Y, which reuses X's bytes. With no data edge between them, only the wait keeps
#      n1 from overwriting X before n0 reads it. Every R[i] must be X[i] + 1.
#   C. Textures on the GRAPHICS ring: n0 samples t0 into t1 (a render target), n1 samples
#      t1 into t2, which reuses t0's bytes. t2 must equal t0's uploaded pattern exactly.
#   D. (4.5.0 audit) A 20-node chain on one ring over 21 buffers that aliasing packs into 2
#      slots, so nearly every node reuses bytes, and the 16 IB slices wrap once mid-graph (the
#      executor drains its queues before reusing them). Every b20[i] must be b0[i] + 20.
#
# Exit codes: 0 pass; 1 ctx; 2 kernel; 3 build; 4 layout; 5 execute; 6 A wrong; 7 B wrong;
#   8 render setup; 9 C wrong; 10 consumer buffers; 11 D wrong.
include "src/lib.cyr"

fn print_cstr(s): i64 { syscall(1, 1, s, strlen(s)); return 0; }
fn print_i64(n): i64 {
    var buf[32];
    memset(&buf, 0, 32);
    var len = fmt_int_buf(n, &buf);
    syscall(1, 1, &buf, len);
    return 0;
}

